-- title:
--   For every pivot in the probability support, mass strictly above its surplus is less than `δ`.
-- statement:
--   For every pivot in the probability support, mass strictly above its surplus is
--   less than `δ`. The same top set, of mass at least `δ/2`, is at least as good as
--   *every* such pivot, even if equal surpluses were ordered arbitrarily.
--
--   This lemma is part of OpenAI's machine-checked proof that rational linear programs can be solved by a strongly polynomial algorithm on a real-number RAM (Smale's ninth problem). It is used in the proof of `OAI.Optimization.LinearProgramming.PriceGame.Charging.exists_quantile_pivots`.
